  "slice_check": {
    "meaning": "All transactions open and all missed sets empty, within the actual held reachable predicates. The exact orbit count of this subfamily gives a constructive lower bound on the whole graph. No depth or full-state count follows from induction.",
    "formula": "(|Val|+1)^K * binomial((|Val|+2)^K + T - 1,T). The per-transaction descriptor specifies for each key either unwritten, or written and its final snapshot from Val union {NoVal}. Transaction permutations turn these descriptors into a multiset.",
    "measurements": [
      {
        "keys": 2,
        "orbits": 7344,
        "labeled": 36864
      },
      {
        "keys": 6,
        "orbits": 8355532713984,
        "labeled": 50096498540544
      }
    ],
    "method": "Append NoMissedOpen == tx = TxId /\\ \\A t \\in tx : missed[t] = {} to the wrapper and configure it as an additional invariant solely to compile its Boolean predicate. With the installed SourceModel, intersect dict(model.properties)[\"NoMissedOpen\"] with induction.load(saved_predicate, model). Use model.state_count(intersection) for labeled states and model.counts(intersection,True)[0] for representatives. Both sizes match the formula."
